1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,650
AI agents are starting to spend money.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:05,750
So who signs off?

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,650
This is Purser, built by Max Geurtsen.

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:12,781
Three Claude agents run a small

5
00:00:12,831 --> 00:00:15,413
company that sells live stock data.

6
00:00:15,463 --> 00:00:19,850
Each has its own Airwallex card, and its own Metal mandate.

7
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:23,279
Inside its limits, an agent pays alone.

8
00:00:23,329 --> 00:00:27,850
Beyond them, nothing moves until the CFO signs the exact terms.

9
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:32,516
Our supplier doubles its price, past the Sourcing agent's cap.

10
00:00:32,566 --> 00:00:35,200
We let one purchase through on purpose.

11
00:00:35,350 --> 00:00:38,850
Metal refused it, and the refusal is on chain.

12
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:44,434
Treasury proposes two ways to stay within the same twenty dollars.

13
00:00:44,484 --> 00:00:46,850
The CFO picks one, with Face ID.

14
00:00:47,350 --> 00:00:49,724
Eighty-six Metal payments in this run,

15
00:00:49,774 --> 00:00:52,850
each its own transaction on testnet. No emulator.

16
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:56,401
Then a customer disputes twelve orders,

17
00:00:56,451 --> 00:00:58,520
all signed by its own agent.

18
00:00:58,570 --> 00:01:01,850
Only the three with wrong data are refunded.

19
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,787
Anything beyond the limits goes to the CFO's phone.

20
00:01:05,837 --> 00:01:09,850
The CFO reads the exact terms, and signs with Face ID.

21
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:13,505
Six seconds later, Airwallex pays the euro

22
00:01:13,555 --> 00:01:15,905
invoice by SWIFT, in its sandbox.

23
00:01:15,955 --> 00:01:17,650
Every I.D. is published.

24
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:20,915
Why not a password?

25
00:01:20,965 --> 00:01:24,075
A password is the same for every payment.

26
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:26,850
The passkey signs these exact terms.

27
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:30,432
Now it's your turn, on the live page.

28
00:01:30,482 --> 00:01:33,978
Claude Sonnet reads the invoice, Claude Opus

29
00:01:34,028 --> 00:01:36,799
advises, and you sign with Face ID.

30
00:01:36,849 --> 00:01:38,250
Then try to cheat.

31
00:01:40,150 --> 00:01:44,100
Change one cent, and the same signature is refused.

32
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:45,850
One cent. Worthless.

33
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,266
All twenty-four decisions by Claude.

34
00:01:48,316 --> 00:01:50,903
Sixteen stops, nothing paid over a limit:

35
00:01:50,953 --> 00:01:54,184
twelve skipped by Claude, two refused by Metal, one

36
00:01:54,234 --> 00:01:57,850
rejected by the CFO, and one planted instruction ignored.

37
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:01,421
Airwallex itself declined two charges:

38
00:02:01,471 --> 00:02:05,018
one over the limit, one in the wrong category.

39
00:02:05,068 --> 00:02:08,850
The agent asked the CFO for a raise, not a retry.

40
00:02:09,350 --> 00:02:14,046
With Airwallex's Airi, agents paid with a single-use Visa credential:

41
00:02:14,096 --> 00:02:16,247
alone within the limit, above it

42
00:02:16,297 --> 00:02:18,242
only after the CFO's Face ID.

43
00:02:18,292 --> 00:02:20,443
Terms changed after that Face ID

44
00:02:20,493 --> 00:02:22,850
were refused before Airi was asked.

45
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,524
The agents do the work.

46
00:02:24,574 --> 00:02:26,850
The CFO signs only the exceptions.

47
00:02:27,350 --> 00:02:31,231
Real: the Airwallex sandbox, Metal testnet, Claude and Face ID.

48
00:02:31,281 --> 00:02:34,850
Ours: the customer, the suppliers, a test second approver.

49
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:38,980
A price shock, a dispute, a euro bill.

50
00:02:39,130 --> 00:02:43,149
Claude decided, Airwallex and Metal held the limits, and

51
00:02:43,199 --> 00:02:46,200
the CFO signed only what went beyond them.

52
00:02:46,350 --> 00:02:47,850
Purser. Starter Kit 11.
